## Project Overview
Arielle's Boutique is a simple e-commerce website for a fictional boutique that sells stylish, affordable clothing. The website allows users to browse products, make enquiries, and contact the store.

## Website Goals and Objectives
- To sell unique fashion items online
- To provide product information and an enquiry form
- To increase brand visibility
- To create a responsive, mobile-friendly experience

## Key Features and Functionality
- Product listing page with grid layout
- Enquiry form for product questions
- Contact page with two locations and maps
- Responsive design (desktop, tablet, mobile)
- Form validation using JavaScript
- Interactive elements for better user experience

## Sitemap
- Homepage (index.html)
- About Us (about.html)
- Products (products.html)
- Enquiry (enquiry.html)
- Contact (contact.html)

---

## Part 2: CSS Styling and Responsive Design

### Styling Features
- External CSS file with reset, base styles, and typography (Montserrat, Playfair Display)
- Layout using CSS Grid (product grids) and Flexbox (navigation, footer, forms)
- Hover effects on buttons, cards, and navigation links
- Consistent colour scheme (purple/blue gradients, red accents)

### Responsive Design
- Breakpoints at 768px (tablet) and 480px (mobile)
- Single-column layout on smaller screens
- Hamburger menu for mobile
- Relative units: `rem` for font sizes, `%` for widths

